<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:144%;">Supplementary Materials for MRO<span id="p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Limitations and Ethics Statement</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Limitations</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose the step-wise group reward optimization (SGRO) approach, which can effectively reduce the reward variance during the reward optimization. However, this introduces new hyperparameters to our MRO, including the size of denoising steps <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> per group and the size of groups chosen for optimizing DLMs in the rejection sampling and reinforcement learning. The selection of these hyperparameters requires careful consideration. To address this limitation, we conduct comprehensive ablation experiments, as shown in Figure <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ D.1 Comparison of MRO with Other Reasoning-Enhanced DLM Approaches ‣ Appendix D Analysis ‣ MRO: Enhancing Reasoning in Diffusion Language Models via Multi-Reward Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. These experimental results provide valuable guidance for selecting the optimal hyperparameters. Additionally, in future work, we will consider designing techniques to determine these hyperparameters automatically.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Ethics Statement</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work does not involve any ethical concerns. All data collected for training our DLMs through rejection sampling and reinforcement learning are sourced exclusively from open-source materials. Additionally, this paper may reference certain case study content. However, these references are presented in an elliptical manner, and any potentially harmful content will not be explicitly presented.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs for Theoretical Results</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the proofs for three theoretical results. The first result shows that introducing a potential-based shaping in reward optimization leads to a higher reward variance. The second result demonstrates that using SGRO can mitigate this issue. The third result proves that our token verification reward encourages DLMs to generate responses with stronger internal sequence correlation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property 1.</span> <span id="A2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under potential-based reward shaping, the expected reward remains the same, i.e., <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[R(s,a)]=\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s,a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[R(s,a)]=\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s,a)]</annotation></semantics></math>, but <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(R(s,a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(R(s,a))</annotation></semantics></math> is higher than <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s,a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s,a))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span>
Let’s denote the original reward as <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and the potential function as <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. The potential-based reward shaping is given by</p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1})-\Phi(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1})-\Phi(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is the discount factor. The expected reward under the potential-based shaping is</p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[R(s_{t},a_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[R(s_{t},a_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1})-\Phi(s_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1})-\Phi(s_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})]+\lambda\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t+1})]-\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})]+\lambda\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t+1})]-\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since the expectation of the potential function at the next state <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t+1})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t+1})]</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the expectation of the potential function at the current state <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math> (because the potential function is a function of the state and the state transitions are Markovian) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[R(s_{t},a_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[R(s_{t},a_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})]+\lambda\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]-\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})]+\lambda\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]-\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})]+(\lambda-1)\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})]+(\lambda-1)\mathbb{E}[\Phi(s_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For the variance, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R(s_{t},a_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R(s_{t},a_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1})-\Phi(s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1})-\Phi(s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}))+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}))+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1}))+\mathrm{Var}(-\Phi(s_{t}))+2\mathrm{Cov}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}),\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1}))+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1}))+\mathrm{Var}(-\Phi(s_{t}))+2\mathrm{Cov}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}),\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1}))+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{2\mathrm{Cov}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}),\Phi(s_{t}))-2\mathrm{Cov}(\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1}),\Phi(s_{t}))\qquad\qquad\quad\quad}_{\text{\footnotesize additional variance introduced by the potential function terms}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:6em;" width="6em"></mspace></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext mathsize="1.140em">additional variance introduced by the potential function terms</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{2\mathrm{Cov}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}),\Phi(s_{t}))-2\mathrm{Cov}(\lambda\Phi(s_{t+1}),\Phi(s_{t}))\qquad\qquad\quad\quad}_{\text{\footnotesize additional variance introduced by the potential function terms}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math> are not independent, the covariance terms are not zero. However, the variance of the potential function terms could add to the variance of the original reward, leading to a higher overall variance. In the general reinforcement learning, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite> has also proven that this result holds when <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s)&gt;2\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s)&gt;2\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite> suggests that such a condition is indeed possible, even when using an optimal baseline reward technique. Therefore, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R(s_{t},a_{t}))&gt;\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R(s_{t},a_{t}))&gt;\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof of Property 1.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Simplified Grouped Reward Optimization (SGRO)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Pre-trained DLM <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>; Group Size <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>; Discount <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>; Learning Rate <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>; Response Length <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Fine-tuned DLM <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each prompt <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> in dataset <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">% Roll-out full denoising trajectory</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{T}\leftarrow\textsc{FullMask}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">FullMask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{T}\leftarrow\textsc{FullMask}(L)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{states}\leftarrow[\,],\;\mathit{actions}\leftarrow[\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑡𝑎𝑡𝑒𝑠</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛𝑠</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{states}\leftarrow[\,],\;\mathit{actions}\leftarrow[\,]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">downto</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             sample <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{t-1}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid p_{0},r_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t-1}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid p_{0},r_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{states.append}((p_{0},r_{t},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑡𝑎𝑡𝑒𝑠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑝𝑝𝑒𝑛𝑑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{states.append}((p_{0},r_{t},t))</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{actions.append}(r_{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛𝑠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑝𝑝𝑒𝑛𝑑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{actions.append}(r_{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">% SGRO: compute rewards and returns per group</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{grad}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑔𝑟𝑎𝑑</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{grad}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">;</span> <math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">;</span> <math id="alg1.l15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\leftarrow g+w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\leftarrow g+w</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="start\leftarrow g,\;end\leftarrow\min(g{+}w,\,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">start\leftarrow g,\;end\leftarrow\min(g{+}w,\,T)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{intra}}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>intra</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{intra}}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Intra-sequence rewards
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow start" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow start</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="end{-}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">end{-}1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{intra}}\leftarrow R_{\mathrm{intra}}+\textsc{TokenVerificationReward}(p_{0},\mathit{actions}[k])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>intra</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>intra</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">TokenVerificationReward</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛𝑠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{intra}}\leftarrow R_{\mathrm{intra}}+\textsc{TokenVerificationReward}(p_{0},\mathit{actions}[k])</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{intra}}\leftarrow R_{\mathrm{intra}}+\textsc{PerplexityReward}(\mathit{actions}[k])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>intra</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>intra</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">PerplexityReward</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛𝑠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{intra}}\leftarrow R_{\mathrm{intra}}+\textsc{PerplexityReward}(\mathit{actions}[k])</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{q}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{q}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l22.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Inter-sequence reward (if final group)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="end=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">end=T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{q}\leftarrow\textsc{TaskAccuracyAndFormatReward}(\mathit{actions}[end{-}1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">TaskAccuracyAndFormatReward</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛𝑠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{q}\leftarrow\textsc{TaskAccuracyAndFormatReward}(\mathit{actions}[end{-}1])</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\mathrm{start}}\leftarrow\textsc{PotentialFunction}(\mathit{states}[start])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>start</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">PotentialFunction</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑡𝑎𝑡𝑒𝑠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\mathrm{start}}\leftarrow\textsc{PotentialFunction}(\mathit{states}[start])</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l26.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Potential-based shaping
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\mathrm{end}}\leftarrow\textsc{PotentialFunction}(\mathit{states}[end{-}1])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>end</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">PotentialFunction</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑡𝑎𝑡𝑒𝑠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\mathrm{end}}\leftarrow\textsc{PotentialFunction}(\mathit{states}[end{-}1])</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="shaping\leftarrow\lambda\cdot\phi_{\mathrm{end}}-\phi_{\mathrm{start}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>end</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>start</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">shaping\leftarrow\lambda\cdot\phi_{\mathrm{end}}-\phi_{\mathrm{start}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{group}}\leftarrow R_{\mathrm{intra}}+R_{q}+shaping" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>group</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>intra</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{group}}\leftarrow R_{\mathrm{intra}}+R_{q}+shaping</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l29.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Group return
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow start" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow start</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="end{-}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">end{-}1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l30.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p\leftarrow\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathit{actions}[k]\mid\mathit{states}[k])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛𝑠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑡𝑎𝑡𝑒𝑠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p\leftarrow\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathit{actions}[k]\mid\mathit{states}[k])</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{grad}\leftarrow\mathit{grad}+\nabla_{\theta}(\log p)\cdot R_{\mathrm{group}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑔𝑟𝑎𝑑</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝑔𝑟𝑎𝑑</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>group</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{grad}\leftarrow\mathit{grad}+\nabla_{\theta}(\log p)\cdot R_{\mathrm{group}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l32.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> REINFORCE update for steps in this group
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l34.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l35.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">% Parameter update</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l36" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta+\eta\cdot\mathit{grad}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝑔𝑟𝑎𝑑</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta+\eta\cdot\mathit{grad}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l37" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l37.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l37.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property 2.</span> <span id="A2.p9.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Using step-wise group reward optimization can reduce the reward variance, i.e., <math id="A2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(R(s,a))&gt;\mathrm{Var}(R^{(w)}(s,a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(R(s,a))&gt;\mathrm{Var}(R^{(w)}(s,a))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{(w)}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(w)}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the reward after applying step-wise group reward optimization.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span>
SGRO groups <math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> denoising steps together and provides a reshaped reward for each group. This means that the number of times the potential function is computed and added to the reward is reduced. Let’s denote the reward for a group of <math id="A2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> steps as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=0}^{w-1}\hat{R}(s_{t+i},a_{t+i})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+w})-\Phi(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=0}^{w-1}\hat{R}(s_{t+i},a_{t+i})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+w})-\Phi(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The variance of this group reward is</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\Big(\sum_{i=0}^{w-1}\hat{R}(s_{t+i},a_{t+i})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+w})-\Phi(s_{t})\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\Big(\sum_{i=0}^{w-1}\hat{R}(s_{t+i},a_{t+i})+\lambda\Phi(s_{t+w})-\Phi(s_{t})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Following the derivation in Eq. <a href="#A2.E21" title="In Appendix B Proofs for Theoretical Results ‣ MRO: Enhancing Reasoning in Diffusion Language Models via Multi-Reward Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}))+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}))+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda^{2}\mathrm{Var}(\Phi(s_{t+w}))+\mathrm{Var}(\Phi(s_{t}))+2\lambda\mathrm{Cov}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}),\Phi(s_{t+w}))-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda^{2}\mathrm{Var}(\Phi(s_{t+w}))+\mathrm{Var}(\Phi(s_{t}))+2\lambda\mathrm{Cov}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}),\Phi(s_{t+w}))-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\mathrm{Cov}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}),\Phi(s_{t}))-2\lambda\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+w}),\Phi(s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\mathrm{Cov}(\hat{R}(s_{t},a_{t}),\Phi(s_{t}))-2\lambda\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+w}),\Phi(s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Compared to Eq. <a href="#A2.E21" title="In Appendix B Proofs for Theoretical Results ‣ MRO: Enhancing Reasoning in Diffusion Language Models via Multi-Reward Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>, we can observe that due to the larger interval <math id="A2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="A2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the correlation between <math id="A2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s_{t+w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s_{t+w})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is typically weaker than the correlation between <math id="A2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big|\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+w}),\Phi(s_{t}))\big|&lt;\big|\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+1}),\Phi(s_{t}))\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big|\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+w}),\Phi(s_{t}))\big|&lt;\big|\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+1}),\Phi(s_{t}))\big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Here, the negative term <math id="A2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2\lambda\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+w}),\Phi(s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2\lambda\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+w}),\Phi(s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math> in the variance expression of <math id="A2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> has a larger absolute value compared to <math id="A2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2\lambda\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+1}),\Phi(s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2\lambda\mathrm{Cov}(\Phi(s_{t+1}),\Phi(s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math> in the variance expression of <math id="A2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, as the correlation between <math id="A2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s_{t+w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s_{t+w})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is weaker. Therefore, we can obtain that this results in a smaller overall variance for <math id="A2.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t}))&lt;\mathrm{Var}(R(s_{t},a_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(R^{(w)}(s_{t},a_{t}))&lt;\mathrm{Var}(R(s_{t},a_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">This completes the proof of Property 2. Here, one problem may arise when only a single group provides a potential-based reward, as the reward that could guide the model toward better token correlation may be lost. Therefore, in this approach, we strike a balance between the reward signal and the reward variance for our MRO. The implementation of SGRO is simple, as illustrated in Algorithm A.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property 3.</span> <span id="A2.p16.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When a DLM is optimized to achieve higher token verification rewards, it consequently enhances its intra-sequence correlation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof:</span> We provide a theoretical proof for the token verification reward by analyzing it from the perspective of mutual information. Firstly, we recall the definition of the token verification reward at the denoising step <math id="A2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R^{\text{tv}}_{t}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t}^{m_{n}}\mid p_{0},r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{m_{n}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>tv</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R^{\text{tv}}_{t}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t}^{m_{n}}\mid p_{0},r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{m_{n}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p17.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\{m_{1},\dots,m_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\{m_{1},\dots,m_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of masked token indices, <math id="A2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t-1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t-1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of the predicted tokens at these positions, and <math id="A2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of unmasked token set. The joint probability over the masked positions can be factorized autoregressively (within the masked set) as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{M}\mid p_{0},r_{t})=\prod_{n=1}^{N}\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{m_{n}}\mid p_{0},r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{M},r_{t-1}^{&lt;m_{n}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{M}\mid p_{0},r_{t})=\prod_{n=1}^{N}\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{m_{n}}\mid p_{0},r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{M},r_{t-1}^{&lt;m_{n}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p17.3" class="ltx_p">where the rest of the sequence is fixed and only the masked tokens are predicted. The token verification reward approximates this joint modeling by computing leave-one-out log-probabilities:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R^{\text{tv}}_{t}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\log\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t}^{m_{n}}\mid p_{0},r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{m_{n}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>tv</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R^{\text{tv}}_{t}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\log\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t}^{m_{n}}\mid p_{0},r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{m_{n}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p17.4" class="ltx_p">Now define the empirical average pairwise mutual information (PMI) among the masked tokens:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{PMI}_{\text{avg}}=\frac{2}{N(N-1)}\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq N}\mathrm{I}(r_{t-1}^{m_{i}};r_{t-1}^{m_{j}}\mid p_{0},r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>PMI</mi><mtext>avg</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{PMI}_{\text{avg}}=\frac{2}{N(N-1)}\sum_{1\leq i&lt;j\leq N}\mathrm{I}(r_{t-1}^{m_{i}};r_{t-1}^{m_{j}}\mid p_{0},r_{t-1}/r_{t-1}^{M})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p17.5" class="ltx_p">Using a standard second-order Taylor expansion around the independence assumption (as in energy-based models), this quantity can be approximated as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{PMI}_{\text{avg}}\approx\frac{2}{N(N-1)}\sum_{i&lt;j}\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{m_{i}},r_{t-1}^{m_{j}}\mid\cdot)}{\Pr_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{m_{i}}\mid\cdot)\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{m_{j}}\mid\cdot)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>PMI</mi><mtext>avg</mtext></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>Pr</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{PMI}_{\text{avg}}\approx\frac{2}{N(N-1)}\sum_{i&lt;j}\log\frac{\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{m_{i}},r_{t-1}^{m_{j}}\mid\cdot)}{\Pr_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{m_{i}}\mid\cdot)\mathrm{Pr}_{\theta}(r_{t-1}^{m_{j}}\mid\cdot)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p17.6" class="ltx_p">Importantly, the leave-one-out log-probabilities computed in TVR serve as sufficient statistics for estimating these pairwise interactions. Therefore, maximizing the average leave-one-out log-probability is first-order equivalent to maximizing <math id="A2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PMI}_{\text{avg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>PMI</mi><mtext>avg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PMI}_{\text{avg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby promoting stronger intra-sequence correlation.
This completes the proof of Property 3.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide additional experimental details and present the experimental results of MRO with reinforcement learning.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Experimental Details</h3>

<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Setups.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For training LLaDA-s1, we used a pre-trained version of LLaDA. The learning rate was set to 2e-5. We trained this model on the s1 dataset for 3 epochs. In contrast to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>, we found that training for more epochs on the s1 dataset did not result in further performance improvements. For rejection sampling and reinforcement learning, we set the learning rate to 2e-6. During training, we performed model validation every 50 steps and selected the best model based on performance on the validation set as our final model. For computing <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\text{tv}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>tv</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\text{tv}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we sampled one token from the predicted masked tokens at each denoising step. For <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\text{ppl}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\text{ppl}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we set <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{ppl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{ppl}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{ppl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{ppl}}</annotation></semantics></math> to 100 and 100, respectively.
In Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ MRO: Enhancing Reasoning in Diffusion Language Models via Multi-Reward Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the x-axis corresponds to the intra- and inter-sequence correlation rewards defined in Section 4.2: the left part presents the cumulative intra-sequence rewards <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\text{tv}}_{t}+R^{\text{ppl}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>tv</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>ppl</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\text{tv}}_{t}+R^{\text{ppl}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the right part shows the inter-sequence reward <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{q}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{q}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. As the reward scales differ, we applied standardization for visualization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training Datasets.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For both rejection sampling and reinforcement learning, we utilized DeepScaleR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> in conjunction with the 10k Countdown<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Jiayi-Pan/Countdown-Tasks-3to4" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/Jiayi-Pan/Countdown-Tasks-3to4</a></span></span></span> and Sudoku<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Ritvik19/Sudoku-Dataset" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/Ritvik19/Sudoku-Dataset</a></span></span></span> datasets. These datasets were randomly shuffled to ensure a well-balanced data distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the evaluation, we focus on five reasoning tasks: GSM8K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>, MATH500 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite>, GPQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>, Countdown<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://github.com/HKUNLP/diffusion-vs-ar" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/HKUNLP/diffusion-vs-ar</a></span></span></span>, and Sudoku<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">6</span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://github.com/dllm-reasoning/d1/blob/main/dataset/4x4_test_sudoku.csv" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/dllm-reasoning/d1/blob/main/dataset/4x4_test_sudoku.csv</a></span></span></span>. During testing, we set the sampling temperature to 0.25.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A3.T4.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:66.4pt;vertical-align:-31.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-82.0pt,15.8pt) scale(0.677800907494988,0.677800907494988) ;">
<table id="A3.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
